{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.tlu.edu/about-tlu/careers-at-tlu/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers at TLU | Texas Lutheran University Skip to content Texas Lutheran University Primary Menu Apply Visit Give To TLU My TLU Academics Admissions Life @TLU Athletics News & Events About Search TLU Home About TLU Careers at TLU Child Pages Adjunct Faculty Administrative Positions Employer Resources Faculty Positions Hourly Positions Volunteer Positions Careers at TLU Texas Lutheran University, located in Seguin, 35 miles from downtown San Antonio, is an accredited university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America. The ELCA’s 26 colleges and universities value and practice academic freedom while preparing students for lives of leadership and service in a diverse world. TLU employs a vibrant family of Bulldogs, each of whom brings their own unique gifts to the table for the common goal of making a difference in the lives of our students, empowering them to live into their fullest potential so that when they graduate, they are equipped to make the world a better place. From our volunteers to our staff and faculty, we value dedicated individuals committed to collaboration, creativity, inclusivity, innovation, and the mission and vision of the university, rooted in education, community, and faith. TLU is committed to equitable hiring practices. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and also are subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Download the TLU Application The application is best viewed in Google Chrome, Safari, or Firefox browsers. Current Openings Faculty Positions Our faculty, from adjunct to tenure-track, benefit from a philosophy of shared governance and a growing university. Faculty Positions Administrative Positions TLU administrators are dedicated to ensuring that students, faculty, and staff all have the opportunity to be a part of our Bulldog community. Administrative Positions Hourly Positions Our employees are the heart of the university, providing great first and lasting impressions. Hourly Positions Volunteer Positions We are looking for volunteers and interns to support various departments across campus. Volunteer Opportunities Student Employment + On-campus employment is available to all students at TLU. Students may apply for the jobs of their choice, keeping in mind their skills, interests, and course loads. Working on campus allows a student to begin building a resume while attending classes. Employment earnings may be used to cover the costs of tuition, room and board, or books and personal expenses. Some students may qualify for Federal Work Study, a classification required for some positions, or may wish to work off campus at various retail stores or restaurants. Students are also encouraged to seek internship opportunities when available in their field of study. More information on the application process, guidelines, and job postings can be found on MyTLU (login required). Food Service Food Service positions are available for students, part-time, and full-time employees through Sodexo. As the largest employer of students on campus, TLU Campus Dining Services understands that work schedules must be arranged around classes, so they are allowed flexibility in hours. Student, part-time, and full-time applications can be obtained by visiting our office in Hein Dining Hall. Equal Opportunity Employer + Texas Lutheran University is an equal opportunity employer. Minorities, females, persons with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. It is our policy not to discriminate unlawfully against any applicant or employee because of age, sex, race, color, religion*, national origin, veteran status, disability, or sexual orientation. Texas Lutheran University will provide reasonable accommodations for applicants and employees with disabilities when such accommodations do not impose an undue hardship on the institution. *Section 702, Title VII, provides that a church-related institution may give preference in employment on the basis of religion where religion is a bona fide occupational qualification reasonably necessary to the normal operation of that institution. As a university of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, Texas Lutheran University will employ persons affirming faith in the mission of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America sufficient in number to maintain an active and dynamic relationship with the Church. Title IX Nondiscrimination Statement + Texas Lutheran University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, or age in its programs and activities. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies : Dr. Bobbi Supak , Title IX Coordinator, 830-372-8019. TLU’s Title IX policies are outlined at www.tlu.edu/titleix. For further information on notice of non-discrimination, click here for the address and phone number of the office that serves your area, or call 1-800-421-3481. In this Section Adjunct Faculty Administrative Positions Employer Resources Faculty Positions Hourly Positions Volunteer Positions Apply Visit Campus Map Net Price Calculator What Academic Field Interests You? Biochemistry Biology Business Administration Chemistry Communication Studies Computer Science Division of Business Administration Division of Education Division of Health Division of Humanities Division of Kinesiology Division of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Division of Social Sciences Division of the Arts Dramatic Media Education (Undergraduate) English History Information Systems Integrated Science Interdisciplinary Studies Kinesiology Master of Business Administration Mathematics Music Nursing Philosophy Physics Political Science Social Innovation & Social Entrepreneurship (SISE) Spanish Theology Visual Arts Alumni | Bulldogs Forever Semester Course Schedules Campus Life Newsroom 1000 West Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 (830) 372-8000 About TLU Offices & Services Campus Equity Careers at TLU My TLU Webmail Library Bookstore Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube TikTok Get in Touch Privacy Policy Website Accessibility Consumer Information File a Report © 2026. Texas Lutheran University. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://www.tlu.edu/about-tlu/careers-at-tlu/adjunct-faculty/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty | Texas Lutheran University Skip to content Texas Lutheran University Primary Menu Apply Visit Give To TLU My TLU Academics Admissions Life @TLU Athletics News & Events About Search TLU Home About TLU Careers at TLU Adjunct Faculty Child Pages Adjunct Faculty Administrative Positions Employer Resources Faculty Positions Hourly Positions Volunteer Positions Adjunct Faculty If you are interested in working as an adjunct faculty member, but there are currently no openings in your field, you may submit your information to be considered for future positions. Use our Adjunct Faculty Inquiry Information Form to let us know your area(s) of interest and expertise. Your information will be provided to department chairs who have open adjunct faculty positions in the area(s) in which you are qualified to teach. Adjunct Faculty Inquiry Form Please complete this form to authorize distribution of your contact information to appropriate department chairs for potential employment opportunities in your area(s) of study/interest. Completed forms will be deleted from the file after six (6) months. This form is not a contract for employment nor a promise of employment for any period or term. It is an expression of interest in adjunct faculty employment only. Apply Visit Campus Map Net Price Calculator What Academic Field Interests You? Biochemistry Biology Business Administration Chemistry Communication Studies Computer Science Division of Business Administration Division of Education Division of Health Division of Humanities Division of Kinesiology Division of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Division of Social Sciences Division of the Arts Dramatic Media Education (Undergraduate) English History Information Systems Integrated Science Interdisciplinary Studies Kinesiology Master of Business Administration Mathematics Music Nursing Philosophy Physics Political Science Social Innovation & Social Entrepreneurship (SISE) Spanish Theology Visual Arts Alumni | Bulldogs Forever Semester Course Schedules Campus Life Newsroom 1000 West Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 (830) 372-8000 About TLU Offices & Services Campus Equity Careers at TLU My TLU Webmail Library Bookstore Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube TikTok Get in Touch Privacy Policy Website Accessibility Consumer Information File a Report © 2026. Texas Lutheran University. All Rights Reserved."
    },
    "https://www.tlu.edu/about-tlu/careers-at-tlu/administrative-positions/": {
      "title": "Administrative Positions",
      "description": "Administrative Positions | Texas Lutheran University Skip to content Texas Lutheran University Primary Menu Apply Visit Give To TLU My TLU Academics Admissions Life @TLU Athletics News & Events About Search TLU Home About TLU Careers at TLU Administrative Positions Child Pages Adjunct Faculty Administrative Positions Employer Resources Faculty Positions Hourly Positions Volunteer Positions Administrative Positions TLU Is An Equal Opportunity Employer Texas Lutheran University employs a vibrant family of Bulldogs, each of whom brings their own unique gifts to the table for the common goal of making a difference in the lives of our students, empowering them to live into their fullest potential so that when they graduate, they are equipped to make the world a better place. From our volunteers to our staff and faculty, we value dedicated individuals committed to collaboration, creativity, inclusivity, innovation, and the mission and vision of the university, rooted in education, community, and faith. TLU is committed to equitable hiring practices. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and also are subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Salary is competitive, with excellent benefits. Current Open Positions TLU Employment Application The application is best viewed in Google Chrome, Safari, or Firefox browsers. Assistant Director of Nursing & Campus Executive Dallas Online + 3/6/26 The Department of Nursing at Texas Lutheran University invites applications for the full-time Assistant Director of Nursing for our new Dallas area online programs. This 12-month position provides leadership and support in the administration of the pre-licensure online Accelerated BSN (ABSN) and Direct-Entry MSN (DEMSN) programs. Reporting to the Director of Nursing, the Assistant Director of Nursing will provide leadership to foster an inclusive and dynamic learning environment and contribute to the mission and strategic goals of the institution. This role requires strong planning, execution, and collaborative skills as well as experience in nursing education and online curriculum development. A strong candidate will be able to coordinate the online programs in the Dallas area, requiring an individual who is a strong leader but also able to stay well-connected to the vision and mission of TLU and the Nursing Program. This position will be critical as Texas Lutheran University strengthens its commitment to student success, retention, and engagement, under a renewed commitment to equity and inclusion. Required qualifications Doctoral degree in Nursing or a related field with at least one graduate degree in Nursing (e.g., Master of Science in Nursing). Current, unencumbered RN license in the state of Texas or eligibility to obtain one. Evidence of at least five years of experience in nursing, with at least two years of nursing education and administrative experience. Responsibilities Work closely with the campus faculty, Director of Nursing, and university leaders to build an environment that is focused on advancing student learning, promoting engagement, and enhancing positive community and climate. Oversee student admissions, retention, and progression on the campus, working with internal and external partners for recruitment and enrollment. Assist in the planning, implementation, and evaluation of the nursing curriculum. Provide leadership in collaboration with the Director of Nursing in meeting accreditation and regulatory requirements. Supervise faculty and staff at the campus, providing oversight for daily work and completing annual evaluations. Work with the VPASA and Director of Nursing to support faculty development and meet the needs of online students. Promote a positive, collaborative, and respectful environment that values civility, innovation, and continuous improvement throughout the department and the University. Build community connections to enhance the Department of Nursing’s academic and clinical partnerships to promote excellence in education. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with a broad range of students, including students from disadvantaged backgrounds and underrepresented populations in nursing. Experience in curriculum design and development, evaluation and assessment, and compliance with state board of nursing regulations and accreditation standards. Evidence of successful experience in obtaining/maintaining nursing program accreditation. Successful experience teaching using a range of formats, including instructional technology, concept-based curriculum, competency-based education, flipped classroom, interprofessional, and team teaching. Experience building and promoting community relationships, including developing partnerships in nursing. Successful implementation of evidence-based practice or research utilization projects. Department Overview Texas Lutheran University (TLU) offers dynamic and comprehensive Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) and direct-entry Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) pre-licensure nursing programs designed to prepare students for a successful career in nursing through flexible campus-based, hybrid, and online formats. With multiple pathways tailored to students’ education and experience, TLU offers the BSN as a traditional program on the residential campus. For students who have a non-nursing bachelor’s or associate degree, the Accelerated BSN program is available in hybrid or online formats that can be completed in 16 months. Additionally, students with a non-nursing bachelor’s degree may enter the direct-entry MSN and complete in as few as 20 months. Both the BSN and MSN include 900 or more hours of hands-on experience offered through labs, simulations, and real-world clinical placements to ensure graduates are confident, competent, and career ready. The Department of Nursing has approval from the Texas Board of Nursing to offer the accelerated BSN and direct entry MSN nursing degrees. The baccalaureate degree program in nursing and master’s degree program in nursing at Texas Lutheran University is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (http://www.ccneaccreditation.org). The curriculum is designed to prepare graduates for a nursing career and requires all students to be involved in evidence-based practice projects or faculty-mentored research. Our BSN and MSN graduates have an excellent NCLEX-RN pass rate and employment rate. Information about the Department of Nursing is available at www.tlu.edu/nursing . “Texas Lutheran University is a Hispanic-Serving Institution with a student body almost 50% Latinx/Hispanic. One of the 26 colleges and universities affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, TLU celebrates its strong religious diversity and its deep commitment to academic freedom. For more information, consult https://www.tlu.edu/about-tlu/equity . TLU is situated at the edge of the Texas Hill Country in the San Antonio-Austin corridor, one of the fastest growing regions in the United States. Primarily undergraduate, TLU also offers a number of graduate programs as well as offsite programs in nursing in Seguin, New Braunfels, Houston, and online in the Dallas area. Salary and benefits are competitive. TLU is an equal opportunity employer (EOE).” Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Texas Lutheran University is not able to sponsor or assume sponsorship of an employment visa for this position at this time. Review of applicants will begin immediately. To be considered for this position, please submit a letter of application addressing the above criteria including teaching and nursing philosophy, research interests, your contribution to health equity, and three professional references (names, addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers). Also include your current curriculum vitae. [Single-file, electronic submission of these materials is preferred.]  Arrange for three confidential letters of recommendation to be submitted separately. Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 Fax: 830-372-6409 Email: humanresources@tlu.edu Assistant Director for Transfer Admissions + 08.24/26 Texas Lutheran University (TLU) is seeking an enthusiastic, student-focused professional to serve as Assistant Director for Transfer Admissions . This opportunity is a great fit for an admissions professional who enjoys building relationships, developing recruitment strategies, and helping students navigate the path to completing their college education. Reporting to the Director for Undergraduate Admissions, the Assistant Director will lead TLU’s transfer recruitment and enrollment efforts for both fall and spring semesters . This position will serve as the primary point of contact for prospective transfer students and will play a key role in developing relationships with community colleges, advisors, students, and campus partners. What You’ll Do: As the Assistant Director for Transfer Admissions, you will: Develop and implement a strategic recruitment plan designed to achieve TLU’s transfer enrollment goals. Lead and own transfer recruitment and enrollment outcomes for both fall and spring terms. Build and maintain strong relationships with community colleges, advisors, and other transfer partners. Serve as the primary resource for prospective transfer students, guiding them from inquiry through enrollment. Advise students and families on academic programs, admission requirements, scholarships, financial aid, and transferability of coursework. Recruit students through community college visits, college fairs, conferences, college nights, and other external events. Lead spring enrollment efforts and collaborate with advising, financial aid, the registrar, and other campus partners to ensure a seamless enrollment experience. Plan and execute campus recruitment events specifically designed to engage transfer students. Review applicant credentials, including academic records, essays, test scores, and interviews, and make admission recommendations. Facilitate campus visits and interviews for prospective students. Partner with TLU’s Nursing program to recruit students, facilitate faculty application review, and support onboarding for students entering the traditional Bachelor of Science in Nursing program. Deliver engaging presentations to prospective students in both small- and large-group settings. Maintain timely and accurate communication with students, families, and campus partners. Help resolve student and family concerns related to financial aid, scholarships, academic programs, admission credentials, campus living, and other enrollment matters. Monitor competitive programs and enrollment trends and recommend strategies to strengthen TLU’s position in the market. Coordinate special projects and other initiatives as assigned. What We’re Looking For The ideal candidate is an energetic, organized, and relationship-oriented admissions professional who is passionate about helping students achieve their educational goals. Required qualifications include: Bachelor’s degree. 2–3 years of higher education or college admissions experience; transfer admissions experience is preferred. Strong customer service skills and a student-first philosophy. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work effectively with students, families, colleagues, and external partners. Strong organization, attention to detail, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently, manage competing priorities, and contribute effectively as part of a team. Texas Driver’s License in good standing. Commitment to the mission and strategic plan of Texas Lutheran University. Preferred qualifications: Previous experience working with transfer students. Experience with Slate or another customer relationship management (CRM) system. Experience with recruitment, enrollment management, or community college partnerships. Work Environment This position is primarily performed in an office setting, with some physical activity and lifting of approximately 25 pounds. Regular travel, including overnight travel, is required , and travel may occur for multiple weeks at a time during peak recruitment periods. Evening and weekend events are also an expected part of the position. Salary and Benefits: Salary and benefits are competitive, including professional development opportunities. Position Application Information: Texas Lutheran University, an accredited university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, is located 35 miles from downtown San Antonio. For more information about TLU, consult our web site at www.tlu.edu. Qualified candidates are encouraged to submit a TLU application, resume, cover letter, and the contact information for at least three professional references to: Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 E-mail: humanresources@tlu.edu A TLU application is mandatory for all TLU applicants. Position will remain open until filled. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until an appointment is made. Texas Lutheran University (TLU) is an official U.S. News & World Report “Best Colleges” selection among regional colleges in the West, ranking fourth on the list for “Best Value,” third for “Best Colleges for Veterans,” and eighth overall. This is the eleventh consecutive year TLU has been featured in the U.S. News and World Report rankings. Other notable recognitions include TLU’s acknowledgment as a “Best Southwest” school by The Princeton Review. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and is also subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Assistant Vice President of Finance and Accounting + 08/24/26 The Assistant Vice President of Finance & Accounting will report to the Vice President for Financial Strategies and Advancement. The Assistant Vice President of Finance & Accounting assists on all strategic and tactical matters as they relate to management of finance, strategic planning activities, investment analysis and implementation, accounting, and tax. The Assistant Vice President of Finance & Accounting provides organizational support and ensures necessary and effective controls and procedures remain in place to safeguard all institution assets and resources The Assistant Vice President of Finance & Accounting will lead the day-to-day operations of the Accounting, Finance, and Student Accounts Teams, while supporting the Vice President for Financial Strategies and Advancement on strategic financial initiatives, and ensuring financial operations are efficient, accurate, and aligned with institutional priorities. They will have direct communication and support responsibilities on matters such as tax planning, compliance, debt structure, banking and cash management, audit and other financial matters. This position will have three direct reports, the Executive Director of Financial Accounting and Budgeting, Director of Accounting, and Director of Student Accounts. Key Accountabilities The primary responsibilities of the Assistant Vice President of Finance & Accounting include: Strategic Leadership: Effectively collaborate with the Vice President for Financial Strategies and Advancement and support institution-wide financial initiatives including bond refinancing, capital planning, major financial analyses, and other strategic projects. Provide operational leadership to ensure successful execution while maintaining continuity of daily financial operations. Financial Leadership: Collaborate with the Executive Director of Financial Accounting and Budgeting and engage with admissions, financial aid and other departments to provide financial analysis supporting tuition and fee pricing, enrollment strategies, financial aid optimization, and institutional planning. Develop meaningful financial insights and recommendations that improve student retention, operating performance, and long-term financial sustainability. Accounting Leadership: Provide leadership for all accounting operations, ensuring timely and accurate financial reporting, strong internal controls, compliance with accounting principles and institutional policies, and successful completion of audits. Partner with the Director of Accounting to establish efficient processes, improve financial close cycles, and strengthen the overall financial infrastructure. Student Accounts & Revenue Optimization: Lead the transformation of Student Accounts by improving billing, collections, payment processes, and communication with students and families. Develop student-centered processes that improve their experience while maximizing tuition collection, reducing receivable risk, and protecting the University’s primary revenue stream. Assist in the effective implementation of the Meadow student account platform. The successful candidate will also: Maintain a high level of communication and collaboration across the Finance, Accounting, and Student Account teams. Identify operational and financial challenges proactively, analyze root causes, and recommend practical, sustainable solutions for implementation. Demonstrate sound judgment, data-driven decision making, and the ability to navigate complex issues while balancing institutional priorities and team dynamics. Manage and hold accountable the Finance, Accounting and Student Accounts teams while building a highly effective finance and accounting organization. Champion modernization of finance operations through process redesign, automation, and technology implementation. Work collaboratively with the relevant Board of Regent committees to provide financial information and presentations that enables effective Board oversight and strategic decision-making. Model the University’s mission and values through collaborative leadership, integrity, accountability, service, and a commitment to continuous improvement. Qualifications: Education A Bachelor’s Degree in Accounting, Finance or related field from an accredited college or university, or related financial management experience is required. MBA and/or CPA considered a plus. Experience A minimum of 10 years of progressive leadership experience is required. Finance experience in higher education or non-profit considered a strong plus Application Instructions: This search is being conducted by Strategic Talent Partners. Interested individuals may reach out to Julie Baker, Executive Recruiter, 763-528-3383 or jbaker@strategictalentpartners.com to express interest, make nominations, and to receive the full position profile. Clinical Coordinator- Houston + 8/17/2026 Texas Lutheran University seeks a Clinical Coordinator for Nursing to lead the establishment and support of clinical nursing sites for our Nursing students in Houston in collaboration with campus leadership. Reporting to the Campus Executive/Assistant Director of Nursing under the leadership of the Director of Nursing, the Clinical Coordinator is a critical member of the Nursing Department and contributor to the success of students’ clinical learning. They are responsible for planning and organizing nursing clinical placements, including networking to identify potential clinical sites. This is a full-time, 12-month exempt administrative position. This role requires strong planning, execution, and collaborative skills as well as demonstrated experience in seeking and establishing clinical sites. A strong candidate will have the ability to connect and build relationships with many different constituencies to support student learning. While not an academic position, they must have a strong understanding of the nursing curriculum and the vision and mission of the nursing program and TLU. Key Responsibilities: The Clinical Coordinator responsibilities will include the following priorities: Identify and operationalize student clinical site opportunities and work with faculty to identify sites and complete onboarding for all clinical rotations. Serve as the liaison and maintain a positive working relationship with clinical sites to facilitate quality clinical experiences that support student learning outcomes. Works with the Director of Nursing, the campus Assistant Directors of Nursing, and the BSN Coordinator to develop and continually refine clinical site strategies. Support students and faculty through the clinical placement onboarding requirements for all partner sites, keeping students and faculty informed. Collaborate to facilitate clinical agreement approval process for clinical sites and validate current contracts for all active clinical placement sites. Promote the mission and vision of TLU and the Department of Nursing among faculty, staff, and students. Other duties as assigned. Position Requirements and Qualifications: The ideal candidate will be a strong leader, skilled administrator, and community builder, creating a strong team at the Houston sites. Specific required qualifications for the position include: Earned Bachelor’s degree in Nursing or business-related field with health care experience. Commitment to excellence in nursing education with undergraduate students consistent with the Department’s Mission, Values, and Program Outcomes. Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills for identifying issues, communicating with stakeholders (faculty, students, staff, and agencies), and obtaining support for the nursing program). Evidence of excellent technology skills including use of Excel, Word and ability to quickly adapt to new technology. Ability to drive to clinical sites to maintain current and build new relationships for clinical placements. Ability to work collegially with faculty and staff in the department and across the university along with external partners. Commitment to university/community service, outreach, and continued professional development. Commitment to attracting, retaining, and supporting students. Understanding and support of the mission of Texas Lutheran University. Preference may be given to candidates who also offer one or more of the following: Evidence of experience in building and promoting community relationships, including developing student practicums in nursing. Evidence of experience in strong teamwork and collaboration skills. Evidence of contributions to diversity and/or experience working with underrepresented student populations, as well as professionals and/or patient populations of such backgrounds. The Department of Nursing has full approval from the Texas Board of Nursing to offer a baccalaureate degree and a direct entry MSN in nursing. The baccalaureate degree program in nursing and master’s degree program in nursing at Texas Lutheran University is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (http://www.ccneaccreditation.org). We have an excellent pre-licensure NCLEX-RN pass rate and employment rate for our graduates. The curriculum is designed to prepare graduates for a nursing career and requires all students to be involved in faculty-mentored undergraduate research. Information about the Department of Nursing is available at www.tlu.edu/nursing . Salary is competitive, with excellent benefits. Texas Lutheran University is affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America. The ELCA’s 26 colleges and universities value and practice academic freedom while preparing women and men for lives of leadership and service in a diverse world. For more information, consult our website at www.tlu.edu . Please submit to: Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 FAX: (830) 372-6409 E-mail: humanresources@tlu.edu Director of Development + 7/20/2026 The Director of Development works in consultation and in close coordination with the Assistant Vice President of Development to design and implement a comprehensive development program to identify, cultivate, solicit and steward prospects and donors for gifts in support of TLU priorities. The specific objectives are to raise annual and major gift dollars to support TLU initiatives, to acquire gifts to support TLU’s endowment, and to enhance educational opportunities for students through academic initiatives and improved facilities.  Funding for this position is available through December 2028. Principal Duties & Responsibilities Identify and qualify prospects with the goal of building and managing a prospect portfolio of a minimum of 125 active prospects. Communicate with existing donors on a regular basis for continued cultivation and retention. Broaden TLU’s philanthropic constituency through fund-raising best practices. Works effectively with boards, faculty, administrators, and volunteers to support programs and strategies to achieve the University’s fundraising priorities. Collaborate with colleagues across the university to fulfill donor goals and objectives and to implement appropriate stewardship and recognition. Participate actively in TLU events. Lead and support any special project fundraising for TLU priorities as assigned by leadership. Travel regularly throughout Texas and occasionally out-of-state is required. Other duties as assigned. Professionalism Perform in an ethical and professional manner. Maintain a professional image. Keep the work environment neat and orderly. Maintain a safe environment through adherence to all safety rules and procedures. Customer Relations Makes visitors feel welcome and respected as individuals, treating them with courtesy and dignity. Exhibits appropriate behavior in customer areas. Demonstrates essential telephone courtesy. Teamwork Work as a team player, supporting and assisting other employees. Identify and participate in resolution of departmental/institutional problems with continuous quality improvement as a goal. Enhance team effectiveness through dependability, accountability and responsibility. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university is required. Position Qualifications At least two years of experience in fundraising or alumni relations. Related experience in development, sales, or public relations will be considered. Knowledge of philanthropy and fundraising principles. Demonstrated experience in establishing and maintaining effective professional relationships with internal and external constituents. Ability to plan, organize, develop, and executive strategies. Excellent communication skills, both oral and written. Ability to manage time and resources effectively. Self-starter with the ability to work independently, to prioritize tasks, and to work with minimal supervision. Ability to facilitate meetings and groups, and to speak publicly. An understanding of and a commitment to the TLU mission. Travel is required.  Must be able to work evenings and weekends as needed. Benefits are competitive.  Texas Lutheran University, an accredited university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, is located 35 miles from downtown San Antonio.  For more information about TLU, consult our web site at www.tlu.edu .  Please submit an application, a resume, and the contact information for at least three professional references to: Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 FAX: (830) 372-6409 E-mail: humanresources@tlu.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until an appointment is made. Texas Lutheran University (TLU) is an official U.S. News & World Report “Best Colleges” selection among regional colleges in the West, ranking fourth on the list for “Best Value,” third for “Best Colleges for Veterans,” and eighth overall. This is the eleventh consecutive year TLU has been featured in the U.S. News and World Report rankings. Other notable recognitions include TLU’s acknowledgment as a “Best Southwest” school by The Princeton Review. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and is also subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Director of Donor Relations and Development Services + Texas Lutheran University invites applications for a full-time Director of Donor Relations and Advancement Services. This position reports to the Associate Vice President for Advancement Services. This position is responsible for creating, implementing, and leading a comprehensive donor stewardship program while providing strategic support for Advancement Services operations. Responsibilities include oversight and support of advancement systems, prospect research and management, reporting, records management, and stewardship initiatives that strengthen fundraising efforts across the university. Serving as the bridge between donor stewardship and advancement services, the Director collaborates closely with the Advancement Services team to ensure data integrity, support the effective use of advancement systems, and enhance the donor experience. Responsibilities Administrative Design, launch, and manage comprehensive stewardship and recognition programs for donors and volunteers at all giving levels. Establish and maintain policies, quality standards, and best practices for volunteer and donor recognition and stewardship. Collaborate with the President, senior leadership, faculty, staff, volunteers, and donors to achieve strategic objectives and deliver appropriate messages for all stewardship efforts. Revise and manage a stewardship communications program, including donor- and volunteer-focused publications that communicate the university’s stewardship programs. Manage the production and distribution of annual stewardship reports to individual donors for ongoing donations, endowed funds such as scholarships and professorships, and major capital gifts to ensure consistency and quality, including the production of an annual honor roll of donors. Oversee the stewardship budget. Research, benchmark, and adopt industry best practices to strengthen TLU’s donor relations programs. Develop and implement a comprehensive system for tracking donor relations activities involving development officers, administrators, faculty, and staff. Maintain a prospect identification and research system that feeds new prospects into major gift and annual giving prospect portfolios. Identify pools of prospects through constituent list segmentation and analysis, electronic database screening, and peer/constituency screening and rating. Maintain a comprehensive prospect rating strategy. Maintain a reporting system for gift officers to reflect pipeline development and metric tracking. Work closely with the Development Services Coordinator on gift acknowledgments and correspondence. Participate actively in the Advancement Team, assisting in creating and carrying out the overall operational and strategic plans for the university. Serve as backup administrator for the Advancement database, providing technical support and ensuring operational continuity. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; master’s degree preferred. Minimum of two years of experience using a fundraising CRM required; knowledge of Jenzabar preferred. Experience in donor relations, stewardship, fundraising, or a related field required. Proficient in using the Microsoft Office Suite. Excellent written and oral communication skills Experience in higher education in a development setting preferred. APRA membership or equivalent professional experience preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Creative, team-oriented, and constituent-focused. Ability to set priorities and manage several projects at once with minimal supervision. Resourceful and self-motivated. Understanding of and appreciation for the mission of a church-related university. Benefits are competitive.  Texas Lutheran University, an accredited university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, is located 35 miles from downtown San Antonio.  For more information about TLU, consult our web site at www.tlu.edu.  Please submit an application, a cover letter, resume, and the contact information for at least three professional references to: Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 E-mail: humanresources@tlu.edu Fax: (830) 372-6409 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until an appointment is made. Texas Lutheran University (TLU) is an official U.S. News & World Report “Best Colleges” selection among regional colleges in the West, ranking fourth on the list for “Best Value,” third for “Best Colleges for Veterans,” and eighth overall. This is the eleventh consecutive year TLU has been featured in the U.S. News and World Report rankings. Other notable recognitions include TLU’s acknowledgment as a “Best Southwest” school by The Princeton Review. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and is also subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Director of First Year Experience & Student Transitions + 8//20/26 The Texas Lutheran University Division of Student Affairs invites applications for the Director of First Year Experience & Student Transitions. Reporting to the Associate Dean of Students for Retention, this position provides strategic leadership for the development, implementation, and assessment of comprehensive first-year and transition initiatives that promote student success, engagement, and retention. Responsibilities: Participate in the implementation of strategic goals for the division that support TLU’s institutional strategic plan. Administer and supervise the First Year Experience & Student Transitions department and staff. Lead the development, implementation, and assessment of comprehensive first-year experience and student transition initiatives. Oversee New Student Orientation, the Peer Mentor Program, Parent and Family Programs, and academic progress initiatives for first-year students. Collaborate with Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, Advising, faculty, and campus partners to support student success, engagement, and retention. Coordinate campus-wide programming that promotes a successful transition for first-year, transfer, first-generation, multicultural, and other specialized student populations. Support coordinated care for students experiencing academic, personal, social, or transitional challenges through collaboration with campus resources. Develop proactive outreach, monitor & intervene in early alert systems, mentoring, and engagement programs that foster student belonging, persistence, and academic achievement. Manage departmental budgets, assessment plans, vendor partnerships, and staffing. Establish metrics to evaluate the effectiveness of orientation, transition, and first-year success initiatives. Prepare reports for senior leadership on student success, engagement, assessment, and outcomes. Utilize data, assessment, and evidence-based practices to guide continuous improvement and strategic planning. Maintain departmental communications, including websites, portal, and social media content Serve on divisional and university committees, task forces, and collaborative initiatives that advance student success and institutional priorities. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Requirements for Position: Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree in Student Affairs, Higher Education Administration, Counseling, Adult Education, Student Personnel, or a related field preferred. Two (2) to four (4) years or more of progressively responsible experience in First Year Experience, Student Transitions, Orientation, Student Success, Retention, or related areas within higher education. Demonstrated experience developing, implementing, and evaluating comprehensive first-year experience, orientation, transition, and student success programs. Strong leadership, organizational, project management, and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Ability to work independently while exercising sound judgment and decision-making Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and campus partners to advance student success and retention initiatives. Ability to establish rapport, build relationships, and effectively support a diverse student population. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal, and presentation skills. Demonstrated experience using assessment data and evaluation methods to inform program development, strategic planning, and continuous improvement. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, including Word, Excel, Outlook, PowerPoint, Teams, and other higher education technology platforms. Ability to supervise, develop, and evaluate professional and student staff. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion when handling sensitive student information. Ability to work evenings and weekends as necessary to support orientation programs, transition initiatives, and university events. Salary and Benefits: Salary and benefits are competitive, including: Professional development support provided. Position Application Information: Texas Lutheran University, an accredited university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, is located 35 miles from downtown San Antonio. For more information about TLU, consult our web site at www.tlu.edu . Qualified candidates are encouraged to submit a TLU application, resume, cover letter, and the contact information for at least three professional references to: Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 Fax: (830) 372-6409 E-mail: humanresources@tlu.edu A TLU application is mandatory for all TLU applicants. Position will remain open until filled. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until an appointment is made. Texas Lutheran University (TLU) is an official U.S. News & World Report “Best Colleges” selection among regional colleges in the West, ranking fourth on the list for “Best Value,” third for “Best Colleges for Veterans,” and eighth overall. This is the eleventh consecutive year TLU has been featured in the U.S. News and World Report rankings. Other notable recognitions include TLU’s acknowledgment as a “Best Southwest” school by The Princeton Review. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and is also subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Director for Graduate Admissions & Degree Completion Programs + 6/24/26 Texas Lutheran University invites applications for the position of Director for Graduate Admissions & Degree Completion Programs . This leadership position is responsible for the strategic recruitment, enrollment, and growth of TLU’s graduate and adult undergraduate degree completion programs. The Director will provide vision, leadership, and operational oversight for all aspects of graduate and degree completion enrollment, from prospect generation through enrollment. This individual will play a critical role in expanding TLU’s presence in the marketplace, building strategic partnerships, and supporting the development of new academic programs that meet the needs of today’s learners and workforce. Key Responsibilities The Director for Graduate Admission & Degree Completion Programs will: Develop and implement a multi-year strategic enrollment plan for graduate and degree completion programs that support institutional growth and enrollment objectives. Lead and oversee all recruitment activities for graduate and adult undergraduate students, including virtual, on-campus, and off-campus engagement opportunities. Achieve annual enrollment goals and key performance indicators established by university leadership. Build and maintain relationships with corporate, community, and educational partners in collaboration with the Office of Strategic Initiatives and Partnerships. Represent Texas Lutheran University at recruitment events, conferences, partnership meetings, and professional associations. Manage the admissions process from inquiry through enrollment, including applicant outreach, credential evaluation, admissions counseling, and interviews. Utilize market research, enrollment data, and industry trends to optimize recruitment strategies, identify new student markets, and inform future program development. Collaborate with the Office of Marketing and Communications to develop and execute marketing strategies that communicate program value, career outcomes, and TLU’s distinct advantages in the marketplace. Supervise, mentor, and evaluate graduate and degree completion admissions staff while fostering a culture of accountability, collaboration, and student-centered service. Plan and execute recruitment events and outreach initiatives that attract prospective students and increase awareness of TLU’s academic offerings. Serve as the primary liaison between admissions, faculty, and program directors to align recruitment strategies with program goals and enrollment targets. Prepare enrollment reports, market analyses, recruitment forecasts, and key performance updates for senior leadership. Contribute to the research, development, and implementation of new academic programs and enrollment processes that support institutional priorities. Coordinate special projects and strategic initiatives as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred. Six(6) years or more of experience in college enrollment management, including supervisory experience. Strong understanding of current admissions trends and strategies. Demonstrated ability to lead teams, manage multiple priorities, and meet enrollment goals. Experience with CRM systems; familiarity with Technolutions Slate preferred. Excellent communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Working Conditions Primarily office-based with a standard indoor work environment. Regular evening and weekend responsibilities. Overnight travel required. Salary and Benefits: Salary and benefits are competitive, including professional development opportunities. Position Application Information: Texas Lutheran University, an accredited university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, is located 35 miles from downtown San Antonio. For more information about TLU, consult our web site at www.tlu.edu. Qualified candidates are encouraged to submit a TLU application, resume, cover letter, and the contact information for at least three professional references to: Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 E-mail: humanresources@tlu.edu A TLU application is mandatory for all TLU applicants. Position will remain open until filled. Review of applications begins immediately and will continue until an appointment is made. Texas Lutheran University (TLU) is an official U.S. News & World Report “Best Colleges” selection among regional colleges in the West, ranking fourth on the list for “Best Value,” third for “Best Colleges for Veterans,” and eighth overall. This is the eleventh consecutive year TLU has been featured in the U.S. News and World Report rankings. Other notable recognitions include TLU’s acknowledgment as a “Best Southwest” school by The Princeton Review. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and is also subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Men’s Basketball Assistant Coach + 08/26/26 Texas Lutheran University invites applications for a full-time Men’s Basketball Assistant Coach. The Assistant Coach provides administrative, instructional, and recruiting support services under the direction of the head coach. Responsibilities include: Assist in planning practice sessions Assist with practice drills during workouts Assist in supervision of weight training program Assist in skill development Assist in recruitment of student-athletes Assist head coach at home and away contests Assist in scouting of opponents Assist in the preparation and maintenance of facilities and equipment Assist in the collection and processing of statistics as indicated Assist with driving for out-of-town trips Exhibit leadership and professional behavior in dealing with student-athletes Accept constructive criticism and evidence professional growth Exhibit good judgment in advising and counseling student-athletes Adhere to the Coach’s Code of Ethics Contribute to the maintenance of good working relationships with all athletics staff members and student-athletes through a positive and constructive approach to all tasks, respect for the competencies of others, and appropriate conflict resolution behavior. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. 1 to 3 years’ experience in coaching and/or athletic administration desired. Strong interpersonal skills. Considerable judgment is required to work independently and make decisions based on precedent and university policy. Ability to work toward general results, devising new methods, modifying or developing standard procedures to meet new conditions. Must be able to maintain confidentiality. Benefits are competitive.  Texas Lutheran University, an accredited university affiliated with the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, is located 35 miles from downtown San Antonio.  For more information about TLU, consult our web site at www.tlu.edu.  Please submit an application, a cover letter, resume, and the contact information for at least three professional references to: Human Resources Texas Lutheran University 1000 W. Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 E-mail: humanresources@tlu.edu Fax: (830) 372-6409 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until an appointment is made. Texas Lutheran University (TLU) is an official U.S. News & World Report “Best Colleges” selection among regional colleges in the West, ranking fourth on the list for “Best Value,” third for “Best Colleges for Veterans,” and eighth overall. This is the eleventh consecutive year TLU has been featured in the U.S. News and World Report rankings. Other notable recognitions include TLU’s acknowledgment as a “Best Southwest” school by The Princeton Review. The University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and is also subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). The university is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and also is subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Apply Visit Campus Map Net Price Calculator What Academic Field Interests You? Biochemistry Biology Business Administration Chemistry Communication Studies Computer Science Division of Business Administration Division of Education Division of Health Division of Humanities Division of Kinesiology Division of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Division of Social Sciences Division of the Arts Dramatic Media Education (Undergraduate) English History Information Systems Integrated Science Interdisciplinary Studies Kinesiology Master of Business Administration Mathematics Music Nursing Philosophy Physics Political Science Social Innovation & Social Entrepreneurship (SISE) Spanish Theology Visual Arts Alumni | Bulldogs Forever Semester Course Schedules Campus Life Newsroom 1000 West Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 (830) 372-8000 About TLU Offices & Services Campus Equity Careers at TLU My TLU Webmail Library Bookstore Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube TikTok Get in Touch Privacy Policy Website Accessibility Consumer Information File a Report © 2026. Texas Lutheran University. All Rights Reserved."
