      "description": "Volunteer Positions | Texas Lutheran University Skip to content Texas Lutheran University Primary Menu Apply Visit Give To TLU My TLU Academics Admissions Life @TLU Athletics News & Events About Search TLU Home About TLU Careers at TLU Volunteer Positions Child Pages Adjunct Faculty Administrative Positions Employer Resources Faculty Positions Hourly Positions Volunteer Positions Volunteer Positions TLU Is An Equal Opportunity Employer Texas Lutheran University employs a vibrant family of Bulldogs, each of whom brings their own unique gifts to the table for the common goal of making a difference in the lives of our students, empowering them to live into their fullest potential so that when they graduate, they are equipped to make the world a better place. From our volunteers to our staff and faculty, we value dedicated individuals committed to collaboration, creativity, inclusivity, innovation, and the mission and vision of the university, rooted in education, community, and faith. TLU is committed to equitable hiring practices. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and also are subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). TLU Volunteer Opportunities Intercollegiate Athletics Volunteer Workers + Complete the following forms: TLU Intercollegiate Athletics Volunteer Worker Position Description Form Non-Employee Athletic Coaches Waiver Completed volunteer description forms and waivers are submitted to program supervisors first for their signature, then to HR. Applicants must comply with the following requirements from Title IX before beginning participation in the program: Complete a criminal background check as directed by Texas Lutheran University. Fill out the Criminal History Investigation Consent Form AND Criminal History Investigation Release , then return them to the Human Resources (HR) office in order for the background checks to be completed. Complete driving record forms provided by either HR or volunteer supervisor (if your volunteer service may require transporting yourself and/or others). This will include providing valid, current driver’s license and insurance information. After paperwork is submitted, the HR office will then request an official report. Complete Texas Lutheran University’s harassment prevention training.Upon clearing background checks, harassment prevention training will be made available through HR. Know, understand, and comply with all applicable Conference and NCAA rules and regulations. Complete blood-borne pathogen and concussion awareness training. Student Organization Volunteer Workers + Complete the TLU Student Organizations Volunteer Worker Position Description Form. Completed volunteer description forms and waivers are submitted to program supervisors first for their signature, then to HR. Applicants must comply with the following requirements from Title IX before beginning participation in the program: Complete a criminal background check as directed by Texas Lutheran University. Fill out the Criminal History Investigation Consent Form AND Criminal History Investigation Release , then return them to the Human Resources (HR) office in order for the background checks to be completed. Complete driving record forms provided by either HR or volunteer supervisor (if your volunteer service may require transporting yourself and/or others). This will include providing valid, current driver’s license and insurance information. After paperwork is submitted, the HR office will then request an official report. Complete Texas Lutheran University’s harassment prevention training. Upon clearing background checks, harassment prevention training will be made available through HR. Volunteer / Unpaid Interns + Complete the TLU Volunteer/Unpaid Intern Position Description Form . Completed volunteer description forms and waivers are submitted to program supervisors first for their signature, then to HR. Applicants must comply with the following requirements from Title IX before beginning participation in the program: Complete a criminal background check as directed by Texas Lutheran University. Fill out the Criminal History Investigation Consent Form AND Criminal History Investigation Release , and then return them to the Human Resources (HR) office in order for the background checks to be completed. Complete driving record forms provided by either HR or volunteer supervisor (if your volunteer service may require transporting yourself and/or others). This will include providing valid, current driver’s license and insurance information. After paperwork is submitted, the HR office will then request an official report. Complete Texas Lutheran University’s harassment prevention training. Upon clearing background checks, harassment prevention training will be made available through HR. The university is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE) and also is subject to the provisions of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 (IRCA). Apply Visit Campus Map Net Price Calculator What Academic Field Interests You? Biochemistry Biology Business Administration Chemistry Communication Studies Computer Science Division of Business Administration Division of Education Division of Health Division of Humanities Division of Kinesiology Division of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Division of Social Sciences Division of the Arts Dramatic Media Education (Undergraduate) English History Information Systems Integrated Science Interdisciplinary Studies Kinesiology Master of Business Administration Mathematics Music Nursing Philosophy Physics Political Science Social Innovation & Social Entrepreneurship (SISE) Spanish Theology Visual Arts Alumni | Bulldogs Forever Semester Course Schedules Campus Life Newsroom 1000 West Court Street Seguin, Texas 78155 (830) 372-8000 About TLU Offices & Services Campus Equity Careers at TLU My TLU Webmail Library Bookstore Facebook Instagram Linkedin YouTube TikTok Get in Touch Privacy Policy Website Accessibility Consumer Information File a Report © 2026. Texas Lutheran University. All Rights Reserved."
